# Every real route is prerendered to its own dist/<route>/index.html by
# scripts/prerender.mjs, so the old "/* /index.html 200" SPA fallback is no
# longer needed - and it was harmful, because it answered non-existent URLs
# with HTTP 200 (a soft 404 that search engines index).
#
# Anything that does not match a prerendered file now falls through to
# dist/404.html with a real 404 status, which both Netlify and Cloudflare
# Pages serve automatically.
#
